VERDICT: FAIL — high confidence.

P1 — No executable-image loader or validation-before-execution path exists.
The contract requires loading already-derived bytes and validating them
before execution (docs/spec/HOST_ABI_V1.md:103-124). Instead,
execute_function accepts canonical LoweringInput, calls lower_function, and
executes the resulting in-memory bytecode
(crates/sley-vm/src/execute.rs:358-370). The purported load test separately
checks emitted bytes, then executes by re-lowering the original program
(crates/sley-vm/tests/rw070_host_abi_freeze.rs:510-536). Corruption and
trailing-data tests only prove byte inequality; they never obtain a loader
refusal (:724-765). Violated rule: axis 3, validation-before-execution and
canonical/derived-state separation.

P1 — Required bindings are claimed but not encoded. The record claims exact
image/profile/epoch/root/import-manifest/limits binding
(conformance/host-abi/v1/host-abi.json:71-102). The cache-key preimage
contains only an adapter-entry count — not an import-manifest digest — and
contains neither image digest, bootstrap-profile digest, nor execution
limits (crates/sley-vm/src/lib.rs:176-210); EXTENDED_V1 fixes that count to
zero (:160-167). The key is derived before image emission and independently
of image bytes/adapters (crates/sley-vm/src/lower.rs:303-338). Limits reach
the observation preimage (crates/sley-vm/src/execute.rs:1411-1421), but
image and import-manifest digests do not. Violated rule: axis 4, exact
bindings / no invented binding claims.

P1 — The admitted import inventory is not closed, although invoked imports
remain default-deny. The specification says only three imports are permitted
and unknown imports reject (docs/spec/HOST_ABI_V1.md:50-73). Resolution
correctly denies unknown identities when invoked
(crates/sley-vm/src/extended.rs:256-326), but judge_bootstrap_profile never
validates every carried adapter row; it inspects reached operations and
resolves only their invoked imports
(crates/sley-vm/src/bootstrap.rs:193-258,348-385). Therefore an unused,
shape-valid, unregistered row can ride the admitted inventory. Violated
rule: axis 2, truly closed positive manifest / admission mechanism.

No additional blocking finding in this bounded pass on layering,
portability honesty, native-helper widening, or minimality. Evidence:
